  "full_text": "So, entertain God and your ass will follow. God wants praise. I thought that zoos and telescopes were really good because they cause praise of God. Then I thought, oh, maybe he doesn't. He wasn't, maybe he's shy. He wasn't really on board. He wasn't like, oh yeah, do that, do that, do that. But, you know, I asked him, his favorite uh his favorite uh toy for a kid and he said a magnifying glass so i think god likes oh if we want to make god happy oh let's go check this out let's go find something that makes mr god happy he wants praise you know i never did this before i never did this before wow look at how look at the color can you see the color Wow. So, I think there's a problem with dignity. This is bad. This is bad. You're in good hands. Bless the Lord, all you his hosts, who serve him in doing his will. What does it mean to say if God is faithful? It means he is steadfast in his allegiance to his people. He will not leave us in the lurch. It also means he is firm in his adherence to his promises. He keeps his word. Faithfulness suggests the idea of loyalty, dependability, constancy, being resolute, steady, and consistent. God isn't fickle. No hot and cold temperature moods with him. God is also faithful to remember his servants. He remembers our works, each individual act. He takes note of the love within us that prompted the deed. No one on earth can do these special things. We forget, but God remembers. We see the action. God sees the motive. This qualifies him as the best record keeper and judge. He alone is perfect and consistently just. You're in good hands with the Almighty.",
